From: sbe1v1k 25.12-6.18 port <noreply@sbe1v1k-build>
Subject: [PATCH] qca-nss-ppe: fix GRE program parser header guard mismatch

The #ifndef guard spells _PPE_DRV_TUN_PRGM_PRSR__GRE_H_ (two underscores
before GRE) but #define and the trailing comment use a single one. GCC
15 enables -Wheader-guard by default and the 6.18 build promotes it to an
error:

  drv/ppe_drv/tun/ppe_drv_tun_prgm_prsr_gre.h:16: error: header guard '_PPE_DRV_TUN_PRGM_PRSR__GRE_H_' followed by '#define' of a different macro [-Werror=header-guard]

Align #define and the comment with the #ifndef spelling. The guard is
file-local, so any consistent spelling is fine.

Classification: portability (compiler warning, no behaviour change).
--- a/drv/ppe_drv/tun/ppe_drv_tun_prgm_prsr_gre.h
+++ b/drv/ppe_drv/tun/ppe_drv_tun_prgm_prsr_gre.h
@@ -14,11 +14,11 @@
  * OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE USE OR PERFORMANCE OF THIS SOFTWARE.
  */
 #ifndef _PPE_DRV_TUN_PRGM_PRSR__GRE_H_
-#define _PPE_DRV_TUN_PRGM_PRSR_GRE_H_
+#define _PPE_DRV_TUN_PRGM_PRSR__GRE_H_
 
 /*
  * GRE tunnel Program Parser configure/deconfigure functions
  */
 bool ppe_drv_tun_prgm_prsr_gre_configure(struct ppe_drv_tun_prgm_prsr *program_parser);
 bool ppe_drv_tun_prgm_prsr_gre_deconfigure(struct ppe_drv_tun_prgm_prsr *program_parser);
-#endif /* _PPE_DRV_TUN_PRGM_PRSR_GRE_H_ */
+#endif /* _PPE_DRV_TUN_PRGM_PRSR__GRE_H_ */
